version 0.3 (unreleased)
========================

* Support python 3.10 to 3.14, django-cms 3.11 to 5.1 and django 4.2 to 6.1;
  drop support for python 2 and older django/django-cms versions
* Replace setup.py with pyproject.toml
* Postprocessors now rely on beautifulsoup4 (optional extra "postprocessors"),
  instead of the python2-only BeautifulSoup 3
* Fix the initial migration for django>=2 (missing on_delete), and add
  migration 0004 (related_name of the plugin pointer, as expected by modern
  django-cms; no DB schema change)
* Stop using django and docutils APIs which are removed or deprecated
* Add a pytest test suite and a tox configuration for all supported versions
* Document syntax highlighting of code via the standard docutils "code"
  directive/role, add the optional "highlighting" extra (pygments), bundle
  a matching stylesheet (static file "cmsplugin_rst/pygments.css"), and add
  "python -m cmsplugin_rst.highlighting [STYLE [long|short]]" to generate
  stylesheets for other pygments styles (docutils uses long token class names)
* Remove the unreachable fallback of restructuredtext() for a missing
  docutils, which would have returned the unescaped source as "safe" html
  (docutils is a mandatory dependency anyway)
* CMSPLUGIN_RST_SETTINGS_OVERRIDES is now read at each rendering instead of
  once at import time, so that it can be changed at runtime (eg. with
  override_settings() in tests)
* A header_level of 0 (allowed by the plugin form) now means "default
  level", instead of producing invalid <h0> tags
* CMSPLUGIN_RST_CONTENT_PREFIX/SUFFIX are now separated from the content by
  blank lines, so that they no longer merge with its first/last paragraph,
  nor break when they end with explicit markup (substitution definitions,
  targets...)
* SECURITY: links and images whose URL scheme is not allowed (eg.
  "javascript:" or "data:") are now neutralized, since they allowed script
  injection by page editors despite the disabling of the "raw" directive;
  allowed schemes can be set with the new CMSPLUGIN_RST_ALLOWED_URL_SCHEMES
  setting. docutils>=0.18 is now required.
* french_insecable() no longer alters the content of code-like html elements
  (pre, code, tt, kbd, samp, var, script, style, textarea), which broke code
  copied from french pages
* Remove a debug print() of the "cmspage" role, which polluted the server
  output on each rendering of a duplicated reverse ID
* Fix "cmspage" docutils role for django-cms>=4: Page.publisher_is_draft was
  removed upstream (draft/publish is now versioned PageContent, not separate
  Page rows), which made the role crash with a FieldError on cms4+. The
  publisher_is_draft filter is now only applied when the field still exists,
  keeping the role working unchanged on django-cms<4.
* Add high-level render_rich_text() utility, usable outside of the cms plugin,
  with optional "header_level" and "report_level" arguments
* Add french_insecable() utility, automatically applied to the html output
  when the page language is french (thin non-breaking spaces before double
  punctuation signs)
* Stop calling prettify() on postprocessed html, since it broke tag spacing
* Add migration 0003 (field help texts, on_delete of plugin pointer)
* Python 3 tweaks
* Reduce the height of the RST textarea in the plugin form


version 0.2
===========

* Add "cmspage" docutils role to get the URL of a djangocms page
* Add "header_level" field in model, to override initial 
  header level for a specific instance
* add default settings for docutils renderer
* add auto replacements for static/media urls, and nbsp/br html elements
* add configuration variables CMSPLUGIN_RST_WRITER_NAME, CMSPLUGIN_RST_CONTENT_PREFIX,
  CMSPLUGIN_RST_CONTENT_SUFFIX, CMSPLUGIN_RST_SETTINGS_OVERRIDES
* fix the case of lone titles/subtitles being removed from output
* switch from South to Django migrations
* add a test project with its sqlite db
* update cms plugin for django 1.8 and djangocms 3.2


version 0.1.1
=============

* support for beautifulsoup postprocessors (CMSPLUGIN_RST_POSTPROCESSORS)
* support for django 1.2 and djangocms 2.1, using South migrations
* initial plugin, with name and RST body